whats the purpose of hybrid_search?

hybrid retrival exist because neither lyxical or semantic search can cover all the things needed
each method has a structural blind spot, so we combine the 2 methods to achieve high precision in search retrieval!

1- BM25 failuers:
BM25 fails to grasp the context, it treats words as arbitrary strings without undestanding its underlying meaning
users rarely use queries that contain the exact terminologt that exists in the documents
and bm25 takes the docs and treat the words inside independetly, failing to grasp the context


2- S-T
a- searching for exact name, like: brand id, certain errors and so on
models often fail to indentifies the exact product ID
like if we searching for a specific error when debuggin our project, "pointer null error 404"
the model might colapse this error into fuzzy clusterss

so single-word queries or exact phrase lookups can produce noisy vectors
pulling in broad thematic matches rather than retrieving the exact words



b- out-of-vocabulary
this is means taht when we pass a word that doesnt exist int he model pre-trained data
so these tokens are recognized in the vectors natively




--> how does hybrid retrieval solve these blind spots?
by runnin bm25 and semantic vectors in parallel and combining their outcomes via fusion algorithms
like RRF or score normalization. hybrid search makes sure to cover the entire spectrum of queries

exacty match query: error 404 setup.py --> hybrid uses bm25 for this
conceptual query: why is my app running so slow --> hybrid relies on semantic search for this
mixed intent: fixing null pointer in this project? --> bm25 identifies the exact project codexion
                                                       while semantic looks for solutions


==> it basically comes down to the the fact that, do we need to retrieve the exact match or a concpetual match!


